IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ei-core`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23) -- from the seat of the insured person: the employee who pays premiums
-- and, on losing a job, claims regular benefits. "Do I qualify? Am I disqualified because of how my job ended? For how
-- many weeks, and how much a week? How much premium do I pay? Must I repay benefits at tax time?" Facts are ones that
-- person can state, mostly from their Records of Employment. The rules are in ei-core.l4; this module builds the
-- answers from plain inputs and restates no rule.
--
-- Unofficial; not an official version. Contains information licensed under the Open Government Licence - Canada.
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Employment Insurance -- the claimant's questions`

DECLARE `EI answer` IS ONE OF
    `the amount, in Canadian dollars, is` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `the number of weeks is` HAS `weeks` IS A NUMBER
    `no regular benefits: I do not qualify` HAS `because` IS A `Qualification`
    `no regular benefits: I am disqualified (s 30)`

§§ `Part I -- qualifying (situation: you have lost or left a job)`

@export How many hours of insurable employment do I need to qualify for EI regular benefits (ss 7(2), 7.1(1))?
GIVEN `the regional rate of unemployment` IS A NUMBER @desc The regional rate of unemployment for the EI economic region where you live, in percent (for example 7.4), as published for the week your claim starts
      `my violations` IS A `Violation` @desc One of: no violation in the 260 weeks before the claim; a minor violation; a serious violation; a very serious violation; a subsequent violation (from a notice of violation the Commission gave you)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many hours do I need for EI` `the regional rate of unemployment` `my violations` MEANS
    `the hours required to qualify` `the regional rate of unemployment` `my violations`

@export Do I qualify for EI regular benefits (ss 7, 7.1, 30(5))?
GIVEN `my earnings were interrupted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have had an interruption of earnings from employment (you stopped working, or your earnings fell below 60% of normal, for at least seven days)
      `my insurable hours in the last 52 weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc Your hours of insurable employment in the qualifying period (usually the 52 weeks before your claim), from your Records of Employment
      `the regional rate of unemployment` IS A NUMBER @desc The regional rate of unemployment for your EI economic region, in percent
      `my violations` IS A `Violation` @desc One of: no violation in the 260 weeks before the claim; a minor violation; a serious violation; a very serious violation; a subsequent violation
      `how my job ended` IS A `How the job ended` @desc One of: laid off, or the job ended through no act of mine; dismissed or suspended for misconduct; left voluntarily, with no reasonable alternative to leaving; left voluntarily, with a reasonable alternative
      `my insurable hours since that job ended` IS A NUMBER @desc Hours of insurable employment you have had in other jobs since you were dismissed or left (0 if none, or if laid off)
GIVETH A `Qualification`
`Do I qualify for EI` `my earnings were interrupted` `my insurable hours in the last 52 weeks` `the regional rate of unemployment` `my violations` `how my job ended` `my insurable hours since that job ended` MEANS
    `the qualification` `my earnings were interrupted`
        (`the hours that count after s 30(5)` `how my job ended` `my insurable hours in the last 52 weeks` `my insurable hours since that job ended`)
        `the regional rate of unemployment` `my violations`

@export Am I disqualified from EI because I was dismissed for misconduct or left my job without just cause (ss 29, 30)?
GIVEN `how my job ended` IS A `How the job ended` @desc One of: laid off, or the job ended through no act of mine; dismissed or suspended for misconduct; left voluntarily, with no reasonable alternative to leaving (for example harassment, a danger to health, moving with a spouse, caring for a child, a firm offer of another job); left voluntarily, with a reasonable alternative
      `my insurable hours since that job ended` IS A NUMBER @desc Hours of insurable employment you have had in other jobs since you were dismissed or left
      `the regional rate of unemployment` IS A NUMBER @desc The regional rate of unemployment for your EI economic region, in percent
      `my violations` IS A `Violation` @desc One of: no violation in the 260 weeks before the claim; a minor violation; a serious violation; a very serious violation; a subsequent violation
GIVETH A `Disqualification answer`
`Am I disqualified from EI` `how my job ended` `my insurable hours since that job ended` `the regional rate of unemployment` `my violations` MEANS
    `the s 30 disqualification` `how my job ended` `my insurable hours since that job ended` (`the hours required to qualify` `the regional rate of unemployment` `my violations`)

§§ `Part I -- how long and how much (situation: you qualify)`

@export For how many weeks can I be paid EI regular benefits (s 12(2), Schedule I)?
GIVEN `my insurable hours in the last 52 weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc Your hours of insurable employment in the qualifying period that count (after a dismissal for misconduct or leaving without just cause, only the hours since then)
      `the regional rate of unemployment` IS A NUMBER @desc The regional rate of unemployment for your EI economic region, in percent
GIVETH AN `EI answer`
`For how many weeks can I get EI` `my insurable hours in the last 52 weeks` `the regional rate of unemployment` MEANS
    LET `weeks` MEANS `the weeks of regular benefits` `my insurable hours in the last 52 weeks` `the regional rate of unemployment`
    IN IF `weeks` GREATER THAN 0
       THEN `the number of weeks is` `weeks`
       ELSE `no regular benefits: I do not qualify` (`does not qualify: too few hours of insurable employment` (`the hours required to qualify` `the regional rate of unemployment` `no violation in the 260 weeks before the claim`))

@export How much is my weekly EI benefit (ss 14, 17)?
GIVEN `my insurable earnings in my best weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of your insurable earnings in your best-paid weeks of the qualifying period: the best 14 to 22 weeks, the number set by your regional rate (22 at 6% or under, one fewer for each point above, 14 above 13%), in Canadian dollars
      `the regional rate of unemployment` IS A NUMBER @desc The regional rate of unemployment for your EI economic region, in percent
      `the maximum yearly insurable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year your claim starts, as published, in Canadian dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my weekly EI benefit` `my insurable earnings in my best weeks` `the regional rate of unemployment` `the maximum yearly insurable earnings` MEANS
    `the rate of weekly benefits` `my insurable earnings in my best weeks` `the regional rate of unemployment` `the maximum yearly insurable earnings`

@export What is the most EI regular benefit I can be paid in my benefit period, counting the waiting week and any disqualification (ss 7, 12, 13, 14, 30)?
GIVEN `my earnings were interrupted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have had an interruption of earnings from employment
      `my insurable hours in the last 52 weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc Your hours of insurable employment in the qualifying period, from your Records of Employment
      `the regional rate of unemployment` IS A NUMBER @desc The regional rate of unemployment for your EI economic region, in percent
      `my violations` IS A `Violation` @desc One of: no violation in the 260 weeks before the claim; a minor violation; a serious violation; a very serious violation; a subsequent violation
      `how my job ended` IS A `How the job ended` @desc One of: laid off, or the job ended through no act of mine; dismissed or suspended for misconduct; left voluntarily, with no reasonable alternative to leaving; left voluntarily, with a reasonable alternative
      `my insurable hours since that job ended` IS A NUMBER @desc Hours of insurable employment in other jobs since you were dismissed or left (0 if none)
      `my insurable earnings in my best weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of your insurable earnings in your best-paid weeks (14 to 22, by the regional rate), counting only jobs that may be used
      `the maximum yearly insurable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year your claim starts, in Canadian dollars
GIVETH AN `EI answer`
`What is the most EI I can get` `my earnings were interrupted` `my insurable hours in the last 52 weeks` `the regional rate of unemployment` `my violations` `how my job ended` `my insurable hours since that job ended` `my insurable earnings in my best weeks` `the maximum yearly insurable earnings` MEANS
    LET `hours that count` MEANS `the hours that count after s 30(5)` `how my job ended` `my insurable hours in the last 52 weeks` `my insurable hours since that job ended`
        `qualification` MEANS `the qualification` `my earnings were interrupted` `hours that count` `the regional rate of unemployment` `my violations`
        `disqualification` MEANS `the s 30 disqualification` `how my job ended` `my insurable hours since that job ended` (`the hours required to qualify` `the regional rate of unemployment` `my violations`)
    IN CONSIDER `qualification`
       WHEN `qualifies (s 7(2))` THEN
            CONSIDER `disqualification`
            WHEN `disqualified for every week of the benefit period after the waiting period (s 30(1)-(2))` THEN `no regular benefits: I am disqualified (s 30)`
            OTHERWISE `the amount, in Canadian dollars, is`
                          ((`the weeks of regular benefits` `hours that count` `the regional rate of unemployment`)
                           TIMES (`the rate of weekly benefits` `my insurable earnings in my best weeks` `the regional rate of unemployment` `the maximum yearly insurable earnings`))
       OTHERWISE `no regular benefits: I do not qualify` `qualification`

§§ `Part III -- my premium`

@export How much EI premium do I pay as an employee for the year (ss 67, 82(2))?
GIVEN `my insurable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc Your insurable earnings from your employer for the year, in Canadian dollars (one employer)
      `the maximum yearly insurable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year, as published
      `the premium rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The employee premium rate for the year as set by the Commission, as a fraction (for example 0.0164 for 1.64%)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much EI premium do I pay` `my insurable earnings for the year` `the maximum yearly insurable earnings` `the premium rate` MEANS
    `the employee's premium` `my insurable earnings for the year` `the maximum yearly insurable earnings` `the premium rate`

§§ `Part VII -- benefit repayment (situation: you received regular benefits in a year of higher income)`

@export How much EI must I repay with my income tax return (Part VII, ss 144, 145)?
GIVEN `my income for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc Your net income for the year under the Income Tax Act, adding back any deductions for EI or CPP repayments (ITA 60(v.1)), social assistance (60(w)) and RDSP or UCCB items (60(y), (z)), in Canadian dollars
      `regular EI benefits I was paid in the year` IS A NUMBER @desc EI regular benefits (not maternity, parental, sickness, caregiving or self-employed benefits) paid to you in the year
      `the maximum yearly insurable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year, as published
      `I was paid regular benefits for a week or more in the ten years before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were paid EI regular benefits for one week or more in the ten taxation years before this one
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much EI must I repay` `my income for the year` `regular EI benefits I was paid in the year` `the maximum yearly insurable earnings` `I was paid regular benefits for a week or more in the ten years before` MEANS
    `the benefit repayment` `my income for the year` `regular EI benefits I was paid in the year` `the maximum yearly insurable earnings` `I was paid regular benefits for a week or more in the ten years before`
